  "narrative": "No assessments are due. I register refinements and probes that target the main unresolved context-dependence signals and possible technical confounding in the supplied lung-lineage composite dependency dataset. First, a KY-library KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction test asks whether the apparently larger KEAP1-loss association among TP53-loss samples, seen in the reversed H53 evidence, is present in an alternative library background rather than only in the dominant Avana context or in co-alteration mixtures. If this KY interaction remains positive with a lower bound above 0.15 units, the co-alteration context dependence becomes more robust; if it is near zero, the earlier signal may reflect confounding by library or co-occurring alterations. Second, a KY-library high-serum KEAP1 interaction test asks whether the borderline H48 attenuation of KEAP1-loss by high serum is also present in an alternative library. Third, an adenocarcinoma-specific high-serum KEAP1 interaction test asks whether serum modification is visible in the dominant biological subtype; this complements the clean genetic-background test H56 and the KY-library test. Fourth, an adenocarcinoma-only PTEN-loss test evaluates whether the borderline overall PTEN stronger-dependency signal is concentrated in the predominant subtype. I retained the original stronger-dependency direction for PTEN-loss because the original raw contrast was in that direction, while the reversed interpretation remains unsupported overall. Fifth, a TP53-loss test restricted to KY screens and KEAP1-intact samples gives a more targeted test of TP53 association outside the Avana library while partially controlling for the possible KEAP1 context effect. This addresses the imprecision in KY and non-Avana TP53 estimates. Sixth, a media 10 versus media 2 main-effect probe broadens the culture-serum technical context beyond the pending 10 versus 5 comparison and can reveal whether low-serum conditions are globally shifted relative to high serum. All proposals remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or external generalizability claims.",
  "research_notes": "Round 4 explore. Current accepted dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4-loss -> stronger dependency, TP53-loss -> weaker dependency, KEAP1-loss -> weaker dependency. These are validated or strongly validated in core contexts. Priority unresolved claims: H54 clean Avana/SMARCA4-intact KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction; H55 adenocarcinoma KEAP1-by-TP53; H56 clean Avana high-serum KEAP1 attenuation; H57 clean no-coalteration PTEN; H25/H29/H40 PTEN follow-ups; H27/H44 TP53 outside Avana; H48 high-serum KEAP1 attenuation; H51/H52/H53 formal KEAP1/TP53 interaction. New registered: KY KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction, KY high-serum KEAP1 interaction, adenocarcinoma high-serum KEAP1 interaction, adenocarcinoma PTEN-loss stronger-dependency test, KY KEAP1-intact TP53-loss test, media 10 versus media 2. Next analyze should prioritize H54-H58 and H57/H60/H61 if cells support, then technical/media/library/omics probes H41/H45/H46/H37/H62, then subtype/age/marker probes only after major robustness questions are clearer. Maintain distinction between supplied-dataset associations and causal or generalizable effects."
